	(text "Four-value read order (per output pixel): v0=(2oy,2ox), v1=(2oy,2ox+1), v2=(2oy+1,2ox), v3=(2oy+1,2ox+1).\nLinear input address: WB = c*H*W + 2*oy*W + 2*ox; v0..v3 add 0, 1, W, W+1.\nColumn step adds 2.  Because H=2*OH and W=2*OW, both a row step and a channel step add W+2 to WB (POOL1: 26, POOL2: 12)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 552 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "86d851a4-bb04-454d-8640-c776ad7b549d")
	)

	(text "Unsigned max rule: MAX is cleared in INIT.  At the first value of every window (V=0) the max register is force-loaded with v0 (UPDATE = CP & (IS_V0 | GT)); v1..v3 are accepted only when IN_DATA > MAX (74HC85 cascade, strict greater).  Equal values keep the current MAX value.  POOL_SEL must be stable for the whole run.\nFSM states: IDLE -> INIT -> {RD -> WT -> CP} x4 -> OUTLD -> NEXT -> (RD | DONE) -> WAIT; RUN is set by POOL_START and cleared at S_DONE.  OUT_WE is asserted in NEXT, after POOL_OUT_DATA has been loaded in OUTLD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 566 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3da62fd5-5a40-4ba4-b3f3-19b47abc78be")
	)

	(text "POOL1: 12x12x8, POOL_OUT_ADDR 0..1151, input 24x24x8 (13-bit address).  POOL2: 5x5x16, POOL_OUT_ADDR 0..399, input 10x10x16 (11-bit address).  Address bits above the used range are still computed to 0 because the window base is cleared in INIT and only legal steps are applied."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 580 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d9502a5-425d-4110-b928-7851c8c43ae5")
	)

	(embedded_fonts no)
)
